infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Node vs Edge runtime: same V8, different physics
  desc Edge isn't faster — it's closer. Pick the runtime by where the data lives.
  compares
    - label Node.js runtime (default)
      children
        - label Cold start 200-800ms
          desc Runtime boot + bundle eval — lands on your p99
        - label Every npm package + native addons
          desc fs, child_process, bcrypt, sharp, classic DB drivers
        - label CPU runs to the platform limit
          desc PDF render, bcrypt cost 12, long crunches all fit
        - label One region, placed near the DB
          desc Each query ~1ms; user pays one long hop on response
    - label Edge runtime (V8 isolate)
      children
        - label Cold start ~5ms
          desc Isolate like a new browser tab — kills tail latency
        - label Web-standard APIs only
          desc fetch, Request/Response, web crypto, streams; no fs/TCP
        - label CPU capped 10-50ms, bundle 1-4MB
          desc Heavy compute and native modules won't fit
        - label 50+ PoPs near the user
          desc Near user but far from central data — RTT per query
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
